      "Normal remodeling supports skeletal repair and adaptation.",
      "Open wound, deformity, bleeding, pain, and possible neurovascular deficits are findings.",
      "Pain out of proportion, pain on passive stretch, tense compartments, and paresthesia are early clues.",
      "Severe pain with passive stretch and paresthesia can precede pallor or pulselessness.",
      "Muscle pain, weakness, and dark urine may occur, though the classic triad is not always present.",
      "Often silent until a fragility fracture, height loss, or vertebral deformity occurs."
